---
// smaqmd-aer-find-ratings — "Where to find an air cleaner's rating", the disclosure
// that tells someone where the CADR / air-flow number actually lives on a product.
// Titled as a statement, not a question: it leads the cleaners step (before the
// fields exist to ask about) and must read the same on the result step's mount.
//
// It is ONE component mounted TWICE (the cleaners step, where the number is being
// asked for, and the result step, where a shopper is about to go looking for one)
// precisely so the two copies cannot drift: the same words, in both places the
// question comes up. Its vanilla twin is the pair of <details> blocks in
// public/aer-tool/index.html — KEEP IN SYNC with those when the copy changes.
//
// COPY IS THE CLIENT'S. The body below is SMAQMD's communications review text
// (Sep 2026) applied verbatim — four steps, one label photo, and no mention of
// "tobacco smoke" anywhere (their note: it reads as irrelevant to someone
// protecting themselves from wildfire smoke, and "use the lowest number" is the
// same instruction without the pollutant taxonomy). Do not reintroduce the
// per-pollutant explanation or the extra example photos without them asking.
//
// Because it mounts twice, NOTHING in here may carry an `id`: two copies of the
// same id is a duplicate-id defect even when only one is on screen. The disclosure
// is esa-collapsible (native <details>/<summary>), so it needs none.
import EsaCollapsible from '@esa/ecology/esa-collapsible.astro';
// The label photo lives in public/ (shared with the vanilla twin), so Astro will
// NOT rewrite its path for the production `base` — withBase() does it.
import { withBase } from '../lib/base';
---

<EsaCollapsible title="Where to find an air cleaner's rating">
  <div class="stack" data-gap="sm">
    <!-- Own list class, NOT the wizard's .smaqmd-aerb__tips: that rule is scoped to
         smaqmd-aer-wizard.astro and would not reach a separate component's markup
         anyway — reaching for it would only look like reuse. -->
    <ul class="typography-body-md smaqmd-aer-find__list">
      <li>
        Look for the CADR (Clean Air Delivery Rate) on the air cleaner's box,
        manual, or manufacturer's website.
      </li>
      <li>
        You may see three CADR numbers for smoke, dust, and pollen. Enter the
        lowest number.
      </li>
      <li>
        If you don't see CADR, look for an airflow rating in CFM and enter that
        number.
      </li>
      <li>
        If your air cleaner only lists Air Changes per Hour (ACH), select
        "Enter Air Changes per Hour instead."
      </li>
    </ul>

    <!-- The label photo — ONE example, per the client's review: three taught the
         same concept three times and made a simple lookup look complicated. The
         other two files (aham-label-100sqft.jpg, aham-label-246sqft.jpg) are still
         in public/aer-tool/ if they are ever wanted back.
         `alt` carries the same instruction the caption does — which three numbers
         are the CADR ratings and which one to enter — because it IS the
         instruction for anyone who cannot see the photo.
         width/height match the file's intrinsic 1200×645 so the box reserves
         its space and the disclosure does not jump when the image decodes.
         IF THE PHOTO IS EVER SWAPPED: update both, and keep the alt locating +
         instructing.
         bcn-lego-checked: no esa- lego is a captioned image/media block — the
         catalog's image-bearing legos are esa-avatar (a circular person chip) and
         esa-empty-state (an illustration + heading + action for a zero state),
         neither of which is a figure with a caption; checked Beacon (no
         figure/media component in its shared ui-* set). So the figure is native
         HTML with a documented smaqmd- block around it. -->
    <figure class="smaqmd-aer-find__figure">
      <img
        src={withBase('/aer-tool/aham-label.jpg')}
        alt="An AHAM Verifide label on the front of an air cleaner box. Under the suggested room size, the section titled Clean Air Delivery Rate Tested lists three circled CADR ratings: 189, 196, and 191. The lowest, 189, is the one to enter."
        width="1200"
        height="645"
        loading="lazy"
      />
      <figcaption class="typography-body-md">
        This label lists three CADR ratings: 189, 196, and 191. Enter the lowest
        number: 189.
      </figcaption>
    </figure>

    <!-- The step-by-step hunt (front of box → side panel → manual → website) that
         used to lead this block, demoted behind a second disclosure at the
         client's request: "box, manual, or manufacturer's website" above tells
         most people enough, and this is here only for the ones it doesn't.
         Nested <details> is deliberate and valid — when the outer disclosure is
         eventually unwrapped (the client also wants this content inline on the
         cleaners step) this becomes the only one, and reads correctly as-is. -->
    <EsaCollapsible title="Need help finding it?">
      <ul class="typography-body-md smaqmd-aer-find__list">
        <li>Check the front of the box — the AHAM Verifide label is usually there.</li>
        <li>Check the specifications panel on the side or the back of the box.</li>
        <li>Check the manual, in the specifications section.</li>
        <li>
          Search the model number on the manufacturer's website and open its
          specifications page.
        </li>
        <li>
          If it only lists air changes per hour (ACH), also note the room size
          that rating was measured in — the tool asks for both.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </EsaCollapsible>
  </div>
</EsaCollapsible>

<style>
  /* Quiet supporting copy — the same rung the wizard's result text sits at, so a
     disclosure opened inside either surface reads as part of it. */
  .smaqmd-aer-find__list {
    color: var(--color-content-default-secondary, #646464);
    margin: 0;
    padding-inline-start: var(--spacing-500, 1.5rem);
  }
  .smaqmd-aer-find__list li + li { margin-block-start: var(--spacing-200, 0.5rem); }
  .smaqmd-aer-find__figure { margin: 0; }
  /* The image RESERVES its box before it loads — the width/height attributes
     give the browser the photo's intrinsic ratio, so opening the disclosure does
     not reflow when it decodes. The token-tinted ground shows while it loads. */
  .smaqmd-aer-find__figure img {
    inline-size: 100%;
    block-size: auto;
    border-radius: var(--radius-md, 0.5rem);
    background: var(--color-background-elevation-sunken, #f0f0f0);
  }
  .smaqmd-aer-find__figure figcaption {
    margin-block-start: var(--spacing-200, 0.5rem);
    color: var(--color-content-default-secondary, #646464);
  }
</style>
